1151: SLPI SEE client, bergamotaslpisee=1 (implies bergamotaslpi=3 and bergamotaslpifrpc=1). After QRTR service 0x190 is up and the FastRPC listener runs
(or failed, or 30 s passed): QMI Control requests with hand-coded protobuf over QRTR (our port 0x4101): SUID lookup of "registry" until the
sensor_process answers, then accel/gyro/mag/proximity/ambient_light, attributes (available, rates, stream type), enable (accel/gyro 50 Hz, mag 20 Hz,
proximity/light on change), indications 0x21/0x22 decoded (no floating point: integer float conversion) into struct bergamota_sensor_sample (accel
counts of a 16 g range, gyro counts of 1/16400 deg/s, mag counts of 0.054 uT, lux, near/far) and bergamota_sensors_post(). Logs the first events, a
10 s rate per sensor, and says plainly when the service gives no response (sensor_process stalled). With bergamotaslpikeep=1 it runs until a fatal
error; otherwise the sensors are disabled at the end of the hold. Requires 1137-1148. Host test: tools/seetest/run.sh.

